 and get some feeling back in your fingers.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3529110/extras/a5e75a1ea4765f3734ded7731a080312.avif?t=1754505414\" width=616 height=90 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3529110/extras/6b2bbe78617eb03b6ea2b5b9aa5a7e2c.poster.avif?t=1754505414\" width=616 height=346 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3529110/extras/6b2bbe78617eb03b6ea2b5b9aa5a7e2c.webm?t=1754505414\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3529110/extras/6b2bbe78617eb03b6ea2b5b9aa5a7e2c.mp4?t=1754505414\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Gathering resources is at the core of surviving in Bushcraft Survival. You'll need to start collecting logs, firewood, bark, and tinder right away if you want to survive this harsh environment.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83e\udeb5 Only carry what you can hold. Larger items such as firewood and logs have a carry limit that you must respect.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udde1\ufe0f While chopping down trees and whittling bark, keep an eye on your tool's sharpness and life. If it becomes blunt, it may break, leaving you without a way to start a fire.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udc1f Fishing and trapping will be your primary way of gathering food resources. Cook on an open fire to rid your food of pathogens and avoid getting sick.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3529110/extras